From: Artzig host adaptation
Subject: [PATCH] PackageUserState: match the nullable splash theme contract

PackageManagerService.setSplashScreenTheme accepts null to restore the manifest
theme. The stored field and getter are already nullable, but the pinned setter
parameter says NonNull, preventing the same call from Kotlin. Correct only the
parameter annotation; storage and change notification remain stock.

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/pkg/PackageUserStateImpl.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/pkg/PackageUserStateImpl.java
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/pkg/PackageUserStateImpl.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/pm/pkg/PackageUserStateImpl.java
@@ -549,7 +549,7 @@
         return this;
     }
 
-    public @NonNull PackageUserStateImpl setSplashScreenTheme(@NonNull String value) {
+    public @NonNull PackageUserStateImpl setSplashScreenTheme(@Nullable String value) {
         mSplashScreenTheme = value;
         onChanged();
         return this;
